+  <dialog id="about" closedby="any" aria-labelledby="about-title"><button id="close-about" aria-label="Close about dialog">×</button><div class="eyebrow">THE ORIGINAL, REIMAGINED</div><h2 id="about-title">A small path tracer.</h2><p>Kevin Beason’s smallpt is an open-source global illumination renderer written in 99 lines of C++. This edition compiles its C++ tracing core to WebAssembly with Emscripten.</p><p>The Cornell box is made entirely of spheres: six form the room, two are mirror and glass objects, and one is the light. Randomizing tints the two objects and the side walls while preserving their materials.</p><p>Rendering runs in a Web Worker, entirely on your device. Each pass adds four new samples per pixel, gradually resolving the noise.</p><a href="https://www.kevinbeason.com/smallpt/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Explore the original smallpt ↗</a><small>© 2006–2008 Kevin Beason · <a href={`${base}wasm/LICENSE.txt`} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">MIT License</a></small></dialog>
